        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Pocket money to planning"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Money from festivals, pocket money, later a salary: how you handle it decides how secure you will be. Personal finance is the skill of managing money wisely."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "budget",
          "income tax",
          "insurance",
          "investments",
          "needs before wants",
          "personal finance",
          "pillars",
          "savings"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Personal finance is how individuals earn, spend, save, invest and protect their money.\nIts pillars are earning, spending, saving, investing and protecting.\nA budget lists expected income and expenses so we spend within our means.\nSavings can be kept in bank accounts, recurring deposits or fixed deposits, which are safe and earn interest.\nInvestments such as shares and mutual funds can give more returns but carry more risk.\nInsurance protects against losses from accidents, illness or damage.\nIncome tax is a tax on a person's income, paid to the government to fund public services.\nNeeds come before wants, and saving a little regularly builds security."
        }
      },
